<section class="section page-hero">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="badge badge-primary">FAQ</span>
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p>Answers to common questions about mirroring websites.</p>
    </div>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What is Website Downloader?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>Website Downloader mirrors publicly accessible static web content — HTML pages, CSS, images and JavaScript files — and packages what it collects into a single ZIP archive you can download.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can I download an entire website?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>You can mirror the publicly accessible pages and linked static resources of a site. Very large sites may hit the download quota or timeout, in which case you should mirror a smaller portion, such as a single page.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Which website resources are supported?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>Publicly accessible HTML pages, stylesheets (CSS), scripts (JavaScript), images and other linked static assets are supported. Private server-side source code and databases are never exposed or downloaded.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can I download private or protected websites?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>No. Website Downloader can only mirror content that is publicly accessible without authentication. It cannot download private pages, login-protected resources, or content behind payment walls.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Where are downloaded ZIP files available?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>Archives are stored temporarily on the server and are deleted automatically after you download them (or after the configured retention period). You must download the ZIP before it expires.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Does Website Downloader download backend source code?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>No. Only publicly accessible front-end resources are mirrored. The server-side source code, application logic, and database contents of a website cannot be downloaded.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Why might some website content be missing?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>Dynamic content that is generated by scripts at runtime, resources loaded behind authentication, or assets blocked by the site's robots.txt may not be captured. Files that fail to download are also skipped.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Is the service free?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes, the current version is free to use. Paid plans are planned for the future and will be announced separately. The site may show advertisements from Google AdSense on content pages; ads are never shown next to the download controls.</p></div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
